+From 66812187789d5417963fd37178ef39b6cdd8ebc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:11:12 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Verifier runtime: a pinned glibc runtime for older
+ userlands, and verify-in-place staging
+
+The Linux guest base (dist-sdshield-2857356cd) is Debian 12 with glibc 2.36; the pinned Helios
+cc962e2b needs GLIBC_2.39 and the helper 4fe0cd3b GLIBC_2.38, so neither starts there (probed in the
+extracted guest rootfs). Rebuilding them would need another toolchain, so the runtime can start those two
+through an exact glibc runtime instead: config glibcRuntime {dir, files, binaries}, accepted only when
+its four files (ld-linux, libc, libm, libgcc_s) equal a tested set in PINNED_GLIBC_RUNTIMES (the build
+host's Arch glibc 2.44 / gcc-libs 16.2.1). Helios runs as <loader> --library-path <dir> <helios>; the
+helper through a private 0500 wrapper in the run directory. The listener keeps its own digest check and
+the host glibc (it needs 2.34).
+
+binaryStaging 'verify-in-place' (default stays 'copy'): for a read-only measured image, where a second copy
+of ~230 MB would cost guest RAM, each file and every directory above it must be owned by root or the
+runtime user and writable by no one else; it is hashed and executed where it is, and leftover children
+are then reaped by recorded identity only. rpc-runtime-main check hashes the glibc files too.
