+From a4bcf90458a2cb43c7f712c9d926e8d142ba5d10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:11:12 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Launch the local chain verifier in the Linux guest:
+ per-host opt-in, gsup service, image inputs
+
+metal/guest/chain-verifier.mjs is the one dependency-free checker of the host operator's opt-in
+(config chainVerifier: the administrator's sequencer pin, 1..16 explicit proof sources, a loopback port;
+no archive - the guest has no curl - and no local cache), shared by the launcher and the guest:
+  * metal/enclave-metal.mjs checks it and passes it through fw_cfg in its checked form; invalid refuses
+    the launch; a direct control guest refuses it (not launched there yet);
+  * gsup.mjs checks it again against the image's pinned runtime (/opt/rpc-runtime/IMAGE.json), starts
+    the runtime as its own supervised child BEFORE the supervisor, and gives the supervisor exactly
+    ENCLAVE_CHAIN_AUTHORITY=verifier and ENCLAVE_CHAIN_VERIFIER=http://127.0.0.1:<port>/, which no other
+    channel may supply. The supervisor is not held back: its verified readers (host wallet admission,
+    platform host policy gate) refuse until the verifier is ready or while no proof source answers;
+    adoption and serving start as before. Present but invalid or no runtime in the image: the verifier
+    authority at a URL nothing serves, so verified reads refuse - never the provider quorum. Absent:
+    no names, no runtime, unchanged.
+metal/chain-verifier-image.json pins what the image carries: the release listener 9ca75047, Helios
+cc962e2b and helper 4fe0cd3b (debug), the glibc runtime two of them run through, verify-in-place
+staging, and the state paths on the guest's tmpfs. metal/overlay-control-image.py installs the runtime's
+import closure, that record as IMAGE.json and the native files from --chain-verifier-dir, refused unless
+each digest is pinned (executables 0555, libraries 0444); without the inputs the image is recorded as
+not carrying them and an opt-in refuses in the guest.
+
+Tests: the checker, env boundary, real launcher (fake QEMU) and gsup wiring; the runtime config the
+guest builds is accepted by the runtime; the overlay's install/absent/mismatch cases; and an end-to-end
+run in the production base image's own userland (Debian 12, node v20, chroot) with gsup's sliced
+supervision, the pinned binaries through the glibc runtime and the supervisor's host admission bundle.
