+From 927e2acfb75486ce94f6e5942fe29df4a2f05dc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:55:47 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Guest image: copy staging; the base is owned by uid 1000,
+ so verify-in-place cannot hold there
+
+The production base dist-sdshield-2857356cd stores 29027 of its 29040 initramfs entries as uid/gid 1000 (node), / /opt
+/app /usr included (receipts/base-owners.json), and the kernel applies those owners when it unpacks it. The runtime's
+verify-in-place rule (the file and every directory above it owned by root or the runtime user) therefore refuses in a
+real guest; the chroot fixture had hidden it (in its user namespace every file appears as root), the install-set probe
+found it. Rather than weaken the rule or rewrite base entries, the image record now uses the runtime's reviewed default,
+copy: each start copies the pinned files and the glibc runtime into its own 0700 run directory on the guest tmpfs
+(/mnt/ramdisk, mounted by init as root), hashes them there and runs them from there. Cost: ~234 MB of tmpfs while the
+verifier runs, on opted-in hosts only. verify-in-place stays in the runtime for a root-owned base.
+
+The guest E2E now asserts copy staging (Helios from <runDir>/bin through <runDir>/glibc, runDir 0700 on the tmpfs) and says
+what it does not model; the image record's unit test pins copy.
